# 21. Performance requirements

The system must remain fluid during common editing operations.

Proposed initial performance targets:

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| Initial interactive editor load | Under 3 seconds on the defined reference device and network |
| Object drag feedback | Target 60 FPS |
| Standard selection response | Under 100 ms |
| Contextual toolbar response | Under 150 ms |
| Local autosave debounce | Within 1 second after activity settles |
| Typical document open | Under 2 seconds |
| Undo/redo visual response | Under 150 ms for ordinary commands |
| Standard export | Under 5 seconds for a typical diagram |

These are product targets, not guaranteed results. The team must define reference hardware, browsers, diagram fixtures, and measurement methodology before using them as release gates.

## 21.1 Large-diagram handling

The application should support:

- Hundreds of objects in ordinary documents
- Thousands of objects in optimized large documents
- Large participant and message counts
- Nested containers
- Complex connectors
- Long editing sessions

Performance techniques may include:

- Incremental rendering
- Viewport culling
- Spatial indexing
- Memoization
- Background workers
- Batched state updates
- Incremental layout
- Efficient hit testing

## 21.2 Memory management

Repeated operations must not produce unbounded memory growth.

Dragging, zooming, reopening documents, and undoing operations should be included in memory profiling.

